# psql: Alpine 3.24.4 (UPSTREAM_IMAGE, pinned by digest) with `apk upgrade` and the PostgreSQL 17 client (psql,
# pg_isready) at PGCLIENT_VERSION, for the migration and partition-runway Jobs that today run postgres:17-alpine
# only for its client tools. The server image's 17.12-alpine3.24 still fails the scan gate on gosu (Go 1.24.6);
# this image has no server and no gosu. The Jobs run their scripts with `sh` (busybox ash); the smoke runs a sample
# of their shell features.
# WATCH_ACTION=retire has no upstream release feed to watch (neither PostgreSQL nor Alpine publishes GitHub
# releases): WATCH_NOTE says when to retire the recipe, and the upstream-watch prints it.
# Bump FC_REVISION to publish a new build of the same pins; an existing tag is never overwritten.
APP_NAME=psql
IMAGE=ghcr.io/figurecollecting/psql
DOCKERFILE=Dockerfile.psql
SMOKE=psql
WATCH_ACTION=retire
WATCH_NOTE="retire when postgres:17-alpine (docker-library) is rebuilt with a gosu that passes the scan gate: scan it with scripts/scan.sh and, if it passes, pin consumers to it and delete this recipe"
DOCS_URL=https://www.postgresql.org/docs/17/app-psql.html
UPSTREAM_TAG=17.12
UPSTREAM_IMAGE=docker.io/library/alpine:3.24.4@sha256:f59abe656b692d901e184be3445e084786602108599d2a51d229c0f5a48c71bf
PGCLIENT_VERSION=17.12-r0
FC_REVISION=fc1
